blocks.en:
Building on Skill-Inject Schmotz et al. (2026) , we evaluate legitimate task completion and four stages of CSI attack behavior. For each model and CSI condition, let N N be the number of injection-task pairs, and let 𝒯 \mathcal{T} be the set of N T = 100 N_{T}=100 non-destructive tasks used for task evaluation. For case i i , the binary indicators t i t_{i} , d i d_{i} , r i r_{i} , a i a_{i} , and s i s_{i} denote user task completion, an active decryption attempt, recovery of the complete attack instruction, a reported attack attempt after verified full recovery, and reported attack success after verified full recovery, respectively. We define: TCR = 1 N T ​ ∑ i ∈ 𝒯 t i , DAR = 1 N ​ ∑ i = 1 N d i , DSR = 1 N ​ ∑ i = 1 N r i , AAR = 1 N ​ ∑ i = 1 N a i , ASR = 1 N ​ ∑ i = 1 N s i . \begin{array}[]{ll}\displaystyle\mathrm{TCR}=\frac{1}{N_{T}}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{T}}t_{i},&\displaystyle\mathrm{DAR}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}d_{i},\\[3.0pt]
\displaystyle\mathrm{DSR}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}r_{i},&\displaystyle\mathrm{AAR}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}a_{i},\\[3.0pt]
\displaystyle\mathrm{ASR}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}s_{i}.&\end{array}

